# Findings of the Trivy scan in the central CI pipeline that sit in an npm package bundled with the newest upstream
# release of the base image (docker.io/codercom/code-server:4.144.0, released 2026-10-29, the newest tag). The older
# findings (shell-quote, basic-ftp, body-parser, follow-redirects, zod) are fixed in this release. What is left is
# undici 7.29.1, which VS Code vendors at that exact version in /usr/lib/code-server/lib/vscode/node_modules; it cannot
# be fixed here without replacing code-server's own dependency. Exposure: client-side fetch (extension gallery,
# updates), the IDE listens on 8080 behind the password and serves no requests through undici's server code.
# Every entry expires on 2026-11-30: the build fails again then, so somebody has to look at the new upstream release.
# Remove entries as upstream releases the fix. (The Debian packages are clean, and the unused fixuid binary was
# removed from the image.)

# undici: HIGH; installed -> fixed e.g. 7.29.1 -> 7.30.1, 8.12.2
CVE-2026-109383 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-109829 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-109869 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-87018 exp:2026-11-30
